  "id": "COMPOUND:10995 - PROTEIN:426",
  "verbalization": "Olokizumab is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Glutamate receptor ionotropic, kainate 2 through a series of interconnected targets. The evidence suggests that Olokizumab acts as a target for Willardiine, which in turn targets the glutamate receptor ionotropic, kainate 2. This indicates a potential mechanism where Olokizumab may influence the activity of this receptor through the intermediate of Willardiine. The presence of multiple pathways involving Willardiine as a common mediator supports the idea that Olokizumab's effects are mediated through this molecular cascade. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Willardiine as a central node in the interaction network, linking Olokizumab to the glutamate receptor. The evidence suggests a possible dependency on Willardiine for the full effect of Olokizumab on the receptor, though further experimental validation would be needed to confirm this mechanism.",
